          "short": "All nonzero terms have odd powers of $x$.",
          "worked": "For each odd power, $(-x)^{2n+1}=-x^{2n+1}$. Hence a polynomial containing only odd-powered nonzero terms satisfies $f(-x)=-f(x)$. Its constant term is zero.",
